@page "/packs"
@inherits ActionPage
@inject PortalApi Api
<PageTitle>Test scenario — Retry Assurance</PageTitle><h1>Delayed response test</h1><p>Check whether a timeout causes a retry to create another job.</p><StatusMessage Text="@Message" Error="@Failed" />
@foreach(var pack in Items){<section class="pack"><div class="title-row"><h2>@pack.Title</h2><span class="tag">@pack.Id@@@pack.Version</span></div><ol class="steps"><li>Your client requests one test job.</li><li>The first reply is held for @(pack.DelayMs/1000) seconds after the job is created.</li><li>A retry with the same key and data gets the same job. A new key creates another job.</li><li>The result checks how many jobs were created and whether the final client outcome is allowed.</li></ol><dl class="facts"><div><dt>Supported request</dt><dd>@pack.Operation.Method @pack.Operation.Path</dd></div><div><dt>Request limit per check</dt><dd>@pack.MaxAttempts</dd></div></dl><p>Use test data only. This scenario covers duplicate creation after a delayed response.</p><details><summary>Version and evidence details</summary><p>Each run keeps its selected version. Different check or scenario versions are not compared as an identical test.</p><code class="digest">@pack.Hash</code><p>Evidence format: @pack.EvidenceVersion · scenario: @pack.Scenario</p></details></section>}
@if(Items.Count==0&&!Busy){<button @onclick="Load">Try again</button>}
@code{List<ScenarioPack> Items=[];protected override Task OnInitializedAsync()=>Load();Task Load()=>Act(async()=>{Items=(await Api.GetAsync<PackList>("packs")).Packs;});}
